## 1. PROJECT IDENTITY

This is a production-grade, pluggable SaaS starter template sold to developers.
Its core promise: "Copy 4 files, add 2 config lines, run docker compose up — your feature is live."

The template is split into zones:
- TEMPLATE zone  → pre-built infrastructure the buyer never touches
- BUYER zone     → the only place buyers add their business logic
- CONFIG zone    → TypeScript and .env files buyers edit to configure behaviour

Cascade must always know which zone it is working in. Never write buyer business logic
into TEMPLATE zone files. Never modify TEMPLATE zone files unless the phase instruction
explicitly says to.

