## 3. ARCHITECTURE RULES — NEVER VIOLATE THESE

### 3.1 Proxy Pattern (Most Critical Rule)
- FastAPI is NEVER exposed to the public internet. Port 8000 is internal only.
- ALL browser API calls go through Next.js API routes which proxy internally to FastAPI.
- The `createProxyHandler` utility in `frontend/lib/proxy.ts` handles all proxy logic.
- Buyers add one line per feature route: `export const { GET, POST, PUT, DELETE } = createProxyHandler('/your-feature')`
- Never call FastAPI directly from browser-side code.

### 3.2 Token and Cookie Safety
- JWT access tokens and refresh tokens are stored in httpOnly cookies only.
- Tokens NEVER go into localStorage, sessionStorage, or any JS-accessible storage.
- Tokens NEVER touch the browser. They live server-side in Next.js and are forwarded internally.
- The browser never sees a raw JWT string.

### 3.3 Single Origin
- Browser only ever talks to one domain (the Next.js frontend).
- There are no CORS configuration changes needed because FastAPI is internal.

### 3.4 Docker Network
- All services communicate on the internal Docker network named `saas-network`.
- Only these ports are ever exposed to the host machine:
  - 3000 → frontend (Next.js)
  - 8025 → MailHog UI (dev only)
- Port 8000 (FastAPI), 5432 (Postgres), 6379 (Redis) are NEVER exposed to the host.

### 3.5 Docker Compose Location
- `docker-compose.yml` (dev) lives at `infra/docker-compose.yml`
- `docker-compose.prod.yml` (prod) lives at `infra/docker-compose.prod.yml`
- All docker compose commands use: `docker compose -f infra/docker-compose.yml up`
- Never move docker-compose files to the project root.

### 3.6 Startup Order (Enforced via depends_on + healthchecks)
```
postgres starts → healthcheck passes
redis starts    → healthcheck passes
     ↓
migrate service runs:
  1. alembic upgrade head
  2. python scripts/seed.py
  3. python scripts/detect_unapplied.py (dev only)
     ↓
backend starts (uvicorn --reload in dev, gunicorn in prod)
frontend starts
```
Never start backend before migrate completes. Always use healthchecks on postgres and redis.

