## 6. AUTH RULES — SECURITY IS NON-NEGOTIABLE

### 6.1 Token Lifetimes
- Access token: 15 minutes (JWT, contains: user_id, email, role, jti)
- Refresh token: 7 days (JWT, contains: user_id, jti)
- Email verification token: 24 hours (stored in Redis, key: verify:{token})
- Password reset token: 1 hour (stored in Redis, key: reset:{token})

### 6.2 Security Rules — Never Break These
- NEVER reveal whether an email exists in any response (login, forgot-password, signup)
- Login failures always return 401 "Invalid credentials" — never "email not found" or "wrong password"
- Forgot password always returns 200 with a generic message regardless of whether email exists
- bcrypt cost factor minimum 12 — never lower
- Password reset MUST invalidate ALL existing sessions across all devices (delete session:{user_id})
- Tokens in httpOnly cookies ONLY — never localStorage, never sessionStorage, never response body
- Email addresses always lowercased before storing or querying

### 6.3 Password Requirements
- Minimum 8 characters
- At least 1 uppercase letter
- At least 1 number
- Validate on signup and reset password

### 6.4 OAuth Account Linking
- When OAuth email matches existing user: show confirmation UI before linking — never auto-link silently
- OAuth-created users: is_verified=true (OAuth emails are pre-verified), password_hash=null
- One user can link multiple OAuth providers

### 6.5 Session Lifecycle
- Login: create Redis session, set httpOnly cookies via Next.js
- Logout: blacklist access token jti, delete Redis session, clear cookies
- Role change: immediately delete Redis session:{user_id} — user is force logged out
- Token refresh: called silently by Next.js middleware when access token expires

