## 7. RBAC RULES

### 7.1 The 4 Roles (Fixed — Never Add or Remove in Template)
- `super_admin` → full access including system settings and role assignment
- `admin` → manage users, bypass maintenance, access all business pages
- `user` → own data, standard business pages
- `guest` → read-only dashboard access only

### 7.2 Permission Table
| Permission         | guest | user | admin | super_admin |
|--------------------|-------|------|-------|-------------|
| View dashboard     | ✅    | ✅   | ✅    | ✅          |
| View own profile   | ✅    | ✅   | ✅    | ✅          |
| Edit own profile   | ❌    | ✅   | ✅    | ✅          |
| View analytics     | ❌    | ✅   | ✅    | ✅          |
| Manage own data    | ❌    | ✅   | ✅    | ✅          |
| View all users     | ❌    | ❌   | ✅    | ✅          |
| Edit any user      | ❌    | ❌   | ✅    | ✅          |
| Bypass maintenance | ❌    | ❌   | ✅    | ✅          |
| Assign roles       | ❌    | ❌   | ❌    | ✅          |
| Delete users       | ❌    | ❌   | ❌    | ✅          |
| System settings    | ❌    | ❌   | ❌    | ✅          |

### 7.3 Enforcement: Check Twice — Both Layers Required
1. **Next.js middleware** (`middleware.ts`) — checks session and role before rendering any page
2. **FastAPI `@require_roles` decorator** — checks role before returning any data

Both must be present. Removing either is a security hole, not a simplification.

### 7.4 Frontend Role Gating
- Use `<CanAccess roles={[...]}>` to show/hide UI elements
- NEVER use inline role checks like `{session.role === 'admin' && <Button />}`
- `<CanAccess>` only hides UI elements — it does not provide security
- Real security is enforced by FastAPI `@require_roles` — never rely on frontend alone

### 7.5 Role Change Effect
- Must be immediate — delete Redis session:{user_id} immediately after DB update
- User's next request fails session check → redirected to /login
- No grace period, no delay

