## 8. FRONTEND CODE RULES

### 8.1 TypeScript
- Strict mode always. No `any` types unless absolutely unavoidable (document with a comment why).
- No `// @ts-ignore` without an explanation comment.
- All props interfaces explicitly typed.

### 8.2 Components
- Named exports for all components.
- Default export only for Next.js page files.
- PascalCase for component names and files.
- All dashboard page components are `'use client'` when they fetch data.

### 8.3 Styling
- Tailwind CSS utility classes only.
- No inline `style={{}}` props unless there is no Tailwind equivalent.
- No custom `.css` files unless the phase instruction explicitly requires one.
- No CSS modules.

### 8.4 Data Fetching — Always Use the Provided Hooks
- GET data → `useData(url)` from `@/hooks/useData`
- POST / PUT / DELETE / PATCH → `useMutation(baseUrl)` from `@/hooks/useMutation`
- Never use raw `fetch()` directly in components for API calls.
- Never use SWR, React Query, or any other data-fetching library — not in this template.

### 8.5 Role Gating in UI
- Use `<CanAccess roles={[...]}>` wrapper — never check roles manually in JSX.

### 8.6 Pre-built Components — Always Use These, Never Recreate
All buyer pages must use these components from `@/components/ui`:
- `PageLayout` — wrapper for every dashboard page, takes a `title` prop
- `PageSkeleton` — loading state
- `PageError` — error state with retry button
- `DataTable` — table with sorting and pagination
- `CreateButton` — consistent add/create button
And from `@/components/rbac`:
- `CanAccess` — role-based element visibility

### 8.7 Navigation and Routing
- Sidebar links are defined ONLY in `frontend/config/nav.config.ts`
- Never hardcode nav links anywhere else
- Route permissions are defined ONLY in `frontend/config/roles.config.ts`
- Never check route permissions anywhere except `middleware.ts`

### 8.8 Auth Layout Behaviour
- If authenticated user visits /login or /signup → auto-redirect to /dashboard
- Middleware handles this — do not add redirect logic to page components

