## 11. CONFIG SYSTEM RULES

### 11.1 Two Sources of Configuration
1. `.env` file — secrets, credentials, URLs. NEVER committed to git.
2. `/config` TypeScript files — behaviour, permissions, navigation. Always committed to git.

### 11.2 Feature Flags (`features.config.ts`)
```typescript
export const features = {
  emailVerification: true,   // false = auto-verify on signup (useful for dev/testing)
  maintenanceMode:   false,  // true = show maintenance page to non-admin users
  registrationOpen:  true,   // false = disable signup (invite-only mode)
  analyticsEnabled:  true,   // false = hide analytics page from sidebar + block route

  // Buyer adds their own feature flags here:
  // paymentsEnabled:  false,
  // multiLanguage:    false,
}
```
Maintenance mode is bypassed automatically for `admin` and `super_admin` roles.

### 11.3 Required .env Variables
These must always be present or the app refuses to start:
`APP_NAME, APP_URL, ENVIRONMENT, DATABASE_URL, REDIS_URL, JWT_SECRET,
EMAIL_FROM, SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL, SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD`

OAuth credentials are only required when their `*_AUTH_ENABLED=true`.

