## 13. BUYER FEATURE PATTERN — THE 4-FILE RULE

When a buyer adds a feature, exactly 4 files are created (plus optional schemas.py):

1. `frontend/app/(dashboard)/business/{feature}/page.tsx` → copy from `_example-page.tsx`
2. `frontend/app/api/business/{feature}/route.ts` → copy from `_example-route.ts`, change 1 line
3. `backend/business/{feature}/router.py` → copy from `_example_router.py`, write logic
4. `backend/business/{feature}/models.py` → define SQLAlchemy table extending BaseModel

After restart, the router is auto-registered. Dev migration runs automatically.
No edits to `main.py`, `middleware.ts`, or any TEMPLATE file needed.

Then in CONFIG zone:
- Add 1 object to `nav.config.ts` for the sidebar link
- Add 1 line to `roles.config.ts` for route permission

